# Every permission the merged manifest may request, with the reason. The build fails on any other
# (constitution Principles I and IX). Only the microphone is a runtime permission.

# Speaking a sentence or a turn (spec 012): asked when the person first taps a microphone; the phone's on-device
# recognizer hears it, and nothing is recorded or sent.
android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO

# Play's asset-delivery library (core/content, spec 012 research R5) unpacks a language pack the person chose to
# download in a foreground service of type dataSync, which it turns on only while unpacking. Google Play asks for a
# declaration of this type at release.
android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE
android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC

# AndroidX core: protects the app's own non-exported dynamic broadcast receivers.
tech.onova.offlinetranslator.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION
